 mods=[
 M('Read the syllabus and policy','Analyse',4,['List the topics, outcomes and hours in the syllabus.','Check National Education Policy 2020 for aims such as competency-based learning, flexibility and holistic development.','Split the syllabus into units of five to eight hours.','Note prior knowledge learners need.'],'A 40-hour physics syllabus is split into five units; unit 2 needs ratio and graph reading from earlier years.','Break a syllabus into units with hours and prerequisites.','Units add up to the total hours and prerequisites are listed.','Why note prerequisites?','Gaps in earlier knowledge block new learning.'),
 M('Write outcomes','Apply',4,['Use one action verb per outcome: define, explain, apply, analyse, evaluate, create.','Add a condition and a standard: with a calculator, within 10 minutes, with 4 of 5 correct.','Order outcomes from simple to complex.','Share outcomes with learners at the start.'],'Apply Ohm\'s law to find the current in a two-resistor circuit with a calculator; 4 of 5 problems correct.','Write eight outcomes for a unit.','Each outcome has verb, condition and standard.','What three parts make an outcome testable?','Action, condition and standard.'),
 M('Plan a lesson','Create',6,['Open with a question, teach in short parts, practise, check, close.','Use two worked examples: one done with you, one done by learners.','Plan the time of each step and the board layout.','Prepare a plan B if time runs short.'],'A 50-minute lesson: 5 minutes starter, 15 teach with example, 20 practice, 5 check, 5 close.','Plan three lessons of a unit.','Plans are timed and each step links to an outcome.','Why use worked examples?','They show the steps before learners try alone.'),
 M('Teach and engage','Apply',5,['Ask questions that need thinking, not yes or no.','Use think-pair-share and cold-calling kindly.','Move around and check work.','Handle off-task behaviour calmly and privately.'],'Question: Why does the bulb dim when a second one is added? Learners think one minute, pair one minute, share.','Teach 20 minutes to peers.','Peers note questions asked and learner talk.','What is think-pair-share?','Think alone, discuss with a partner, share with the class.'),
 M('Assess fairly','Evaluate',6,['Make a test blueprint: outcomes against question types and marks.','Write clear questions with one task each.','Use a marking scheme and a rubric for written answers.','Give feedback within a week.'],'A 20-mark test: 4 marks recall, 8 marks apply, 8 marks analyse across four outcomes.','Write a test and its marking scheme.','Test matches the blueprint and the marking scheme is clear.','What is a test blueprint?','A plan showing outcomes, question types and marks.'),
 M('Use results to teach better','Analyse',5,['Count how many learners got each question right.','Find questions most learners missed and look for the cause.','Group learners by need.','Plan reteaching and tutoring goals.'],'Question 4 missed by 70% because the unit conversion was not taught; add a ten-minute mini-lesson.','Analyse results of ten learners.','Findings link to specific actions.','What does item analysis show?','Which questions learners found hard and why.'),
 M('Tutor one to one','Apply',5,['Diagnose first: ask the learner to explain or solve a problem aloud.','Set a small goal for the session.','Teach a step, let the learner try, give feedback.','Keep a short progress note after each session.'],'A 30-minute session: five minutes diagnosing fractions, fifteen minutes on common denominators, ten minutes on practice.','Run two tutoring sessions and write notes.','Goals are small and notes show progress.','What comes before teaching in tutoring?','Diagnosing what the learner already knows.'),
 M('Capstone: six-lesson unit','Create',5,['Write outcomes, six lesson plans and a test.','Teach at least one lesson with a mentor.','Analyse the test.','Write the reteaching and tutoring plan.'],'A six-lesson unit on circuits with a 20-mark test and a tutoring plan for two learners.','Present the unit and the analysis.','Unit is coherent, test matches the blueprint and plan uses the results.','What proves the unit worked?','Test results and a reteaching plan based on them.')],
 extra=[('Why give feedback quickly?','Learners can use it while the work is fresh.'),('What is differentiation?','Adapting tasks to different learners.')],
